        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'House of Cards',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "House of Cards is a dual-purpose term. While it commonly refers to the physical act of building towers with playing cards, it is also a specific, traditional drawing and building game. In its game form, players compete to build virtual 'rooms' and 'stories' by matching colors and ranks to score points based on triangle formations.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Derived from architectural parlor games of the 18th century, where cards were used as visual aids or components for geometric challenges.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two players. Each player is assigned a color (Red or Black) in the common half-deck variant; with the full deck both take turns placing cards to build the shared house structure.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck. Often split by color (Red vs Black).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck. Often split by color (Red vs Black).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Players draw cards to their hand (usually 3 at a time) to build their 'house'.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Half deck: Use 26 cards (e.g. Red vs Black); each player is assigned a color.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Collapse variant: A player may force a collapse when unable to win; the opponent who last placed a card incurs a penalty.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Other variants: House rules may vary initial deal size, scoring of ties, or number of cards per draw.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
